menu "Smart Doorbell application"

config SMART_DOORBELL_PRODUCTION_APP
    bool "Build the event-driven production application"
    default n
    help
        Enable the C++ wake/capture/upload/deep-sleep controller. Leave this
        disabled during hardware bring-up so the core-only safe image remains
        the default.

config SMART_DOORBELL_ENABLE_PIR_EVENTS
    bool "Enable PIR-triggered production events"
    depends on SMART_DOORBELL_PRODUCTION_APP
    default n
    help
        Arm GPIO3 as a production wake source and generate PIR_MOTION events.
        Leave this disabled for the normal button-only doorbell flow. The
        isolated wake diagnostic can still exercise PIR independently.

config SMART_DOORBELL_WAKE_SLEEP_DIAGNOSTIC
    bool "Build the button/PIR wake and deep-sleep diagnostic"
    default n
    help
        Build a bounded wake-only image. It never starts the camera, Wi-Fi,
        MQTT, amplifier, or I2S and returns to deep sleep after reporting the
        wake cause.

config SMART_DOORBELL_MIC_DIAGNOSTIC
    bool "Build the USB-powered MK1 microphone diagnostic"
    depends on !SMART_DOORBELL_PRODUCTION_APP && !SMART_DOORBELL_WAKE_SLEEP_DIAGNOSTIC
    default n
    help
        Build the isolated ICS-43434 I2S receive diagnostic. It keeps the
        camera, Wi-Fi, MQTT, speaker output, amplifier, and deep sleep
        disabled, then reports per-slot sample range and average magnitude.
        Use USB power only while investigating the Rev C battery-start fault.

endmenu
